INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Conti public attribution, leaks, and DOJ case page", "source_url": "https://rewardsforjustice.net/rewards/conti/; https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2022/03/01/conti-ransomware-group-internal-chats-leaked-over-russia-ukraine-conflict/; https://www.cisecurity.org/insights/blog/the-conti-leaks-a-case-of-cybercrimes-commercialization; https://www.justice.gov/usao-mdtn/conti-ransomware-2", "text": "Evidence batch: Rewards for Justice describes Conti, also known as Wizard Spider, as a Russian government-linked ransomware-as-a-service group targeting US and Western critical infrastructure. It says aliases Target, Reshaev, Professor, Tramp, and Dandis are believed linked to Conti; associated location Russia; associated applications include Conti ransomware-as-a-service, TrickBot, IcedID, Cobalt Strike, and ZLoader. It reports first detection in 2019, more than 1,000 operations, over 400 organizations worldwide victimized and over 290 in the US, with theft and encryption, ransom portals, and publication/sale of stolen data if unpaid; demands up to $25m. It says operators pledged support to Russia after February 2022 invasion and threatened infrastructure of countries perceived hostile to Russia. Rapid7 reports @ContiLeaks released 14MB of chats in 393 JSON files on Feb 27, 2022; some encrypted, so incomplete. Leaks included internal communications, tools, exploits/design processes, credentials, alleged server access, and alleged source code; Rapid7 says the leaker was likely a senior member or coalition of disgruntled affiliates. Rapid7 describes hiring/interviews, coding exercises, salary negotiations, product development, Bitcoin holdings, alleged FSB funding discussion, coders, testers, phishing, control panel, operators, third-party malicious documents, and ongoing operations after infrastructure takedown. CIS reports Conti as a notorious RaaS using double extortion and possible ties to TrickBot; leaks described business units and specialized roles: Coders, Testers, Administrators, Reverse Engineers, Penetration Testers/Hackers, with spamming contracted out; more than 60 employees claimed by an insider in July 2021. CIS says Conti platform shut down/rebranded into smaller units in May 2022 and leak/negotiation infrastructure shut down about a month later. CIS explains RaaS as developers leasing malware to affiliates who conduct intrusions and share profits, often 70/30, and initial access brokers selling access. DOJ Middle District of Tennessee page lists cases 3:23-CR-00092 against Maksim Galochkin, Maksim Rudenskiy, Mikhail Tsarev, Andrey Zhuykov, and 3:23-CR-00088 against Oleksii Lytvynenko. DOJ says Conti affected more than 900 victims worldwide; the four 2023 defendants are charged with CFAA and wire-fraud conspiracies, and Lytvynenko is charged with conspiracy to deploy Conti. DOJ explicitly says defendants are presumed innocent. As of June 10, 2026 DOJ page says Lytvynenko pleaded guilty to Count 2 conspiracy to commit wire fraud, with sentencing scheduled Sept 10, 2026."}
